1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,690
"Abnormal semen analysis…

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:06,680
Well, that's it, it's over,
my bloodline ends right here!

3
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:10,600
Honey, go water the begonia in the
living room—that flowerpot is our

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,900
only heir now!"

5
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:16,980
That is the exact disaster movie that
plays in every guy's head the second he

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:21,650
opens his results. Except science
tells a completely different story:

7
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:25,120
a number below the limit
is not a courtroom verdict.

8
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,910
It's an orange check-engine
light on your dashboard.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,020
When it lights up, you don't set the
car on fire on the side of the highway—

10
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:34,230
you pop the hood and check it out!

11
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:37,700
I am Doctor Senai Aksoy,
fertility specialist.

12
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:42,480
In this video: what those famous
"normal ranges" actually hide,

13
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:46,730
why you shouldn't draft your last will
and testament after a single test,

14
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:50,870
and when it's time to see a
urologist or an andrologist.

15
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,700
First, picture the scene.

16
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:57,620
The result hits your phone: a two-page
PDF that you open standing in the

17
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,540
kitchen, right next to the fridge.

18
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,920
Why always standing in
front of the fridge?

19
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:05,880
Because a man always takes bad
news standing next to the yogurts.

20
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:09,400
On the left, Latin.
In the middle, numbers.

21
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:13,300
And on the right… little asterisks,
arrows nose-diving,

22
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:18,720
and bold text. A lab report is the only
document on earth where you actually pay

23
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:23,690
money to get yelled at in bold font
without anyone ever explaining why!

24
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:28,520
And right then, the universal male
reflex kicks in: the two-finger

25
00:01:28,560 --> 00:01:32,210
pinch-and-zoom! Like you're scouting
real estate on Google Earth!

26
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:36,460
Buddy, zooming in on a PDF
has never spawned extra sperm—

27
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,280
it just makes the pixels bigger!

28
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:42,080
"Hang on, let me zoom in a little more,
maybe there are four of them playing

29
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,540
poker behind the margin…"

30
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:46,930
From the living room,
your partner calls out: "So?"

31
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:50,500
And all that comes out
of your mouth is: "So…

32
00:01:50,540 --> 00:01:54,420
there are stars. I think we just
automatically qualified for the

33
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:55,340
Champions League."

34
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:59,710
At the very bottom, the finishing
move in twenty-eight letters:

35
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:03,000
"oligo-astheno-teratozoospermia."

36
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:06,620
If you can pronounce that in
one breath without passing out,

37
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:09,310
they hand you a urology
degree on the spot!

38
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:13,880
With the screen zoomed in, the word
doesn't even fit on the phone anymore—

39
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:16,850
it's spilling over into the
neighbor's Wi-Fi network!

40
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:20,730
Faced with a number,
human nature looks for a sentence.

41
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:26,620
Yet since 2021, the World Health
Organization (WHO) has put it in

42
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:32,180
black and white: for any given man, a
semen analysis never predicts fertility on

43
00:02:32,220 --> 00:02:35,720
its own. What matters is
the fertility of the couple.

44
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:39,830
Clearly, the PDF hasn't installed
that software update yet.

45
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:42,840
Let's quickly translate
that monster of a word.

46
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:48,280
It's not an ancient pharaonic curse; it's
just a summary of three criteria under

47
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,130
the microscope:

48
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:53,310
Concentration: how crowded
the room is per milliliter.

49
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,610
(Oligo: Well, the club is a bit
empty, there's an echo in here.)

50
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,010
Motility: how many are
swimming straight ahead.

51
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:03,430
In medicine, we call them "progressive."

52
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,050
Nothing to do with politics!

53
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:09,860
Don't look at the sheet and say, "Oh
great, my guys are progressive liberals,

54
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:14,400
very open-minded!" (Astheno:
The boys are exhausted, they're just

55
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:15,350
treading water.)

56
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:19,030
Morphology: how many
have movie-star looks.

57
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:24,400
(Terato: Okay, they look like they just
stumbled out of a nightclub at 4 AM.)

58
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:29,020
First real question: where do these
"normal ranges" even come from?

59
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:33,920
People often picture five professors in
Geneva sipping espresso and declaring:

60
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:37,820
"Gentlemen, the ideal sperm
must look like Brad Pitt."

61
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:43,280
Not at all! The WHO gathered results
from thousands of men across five

62
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,580
continents. What did they have in common?

63
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:49,370
Their partners had all gotten
pregnant in less than a year.

64
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,290
Certified future dads.

65
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:56,200
Picture a giant class photo where all
these dads are lined up from the lowest

66
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,560
number to the highest.

67
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:02,660
The WHO threshold is just a line drawn
at the very bottom of that photo.

68
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,120
(The exact values are
on screen right now.)

69
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,340
Guess how many future fathers are below

70
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:08,930
that line? Zero?

71
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,820
Five out of a hundred!

72
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:15,100
By definition! Five percent of
those men "failed" on paper…

73
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:18,840
while they were literally assembling
a stroller in the living room!

74
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:22,860
Why? Because this isn't a
medical school entrance exam—

75
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:25,510
it's just the front
row of the class photo!

76
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:28,600
So which number crushes morale the most?

77
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:31,040
Almost always morphology.

78
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:36,220
Out of a hundred sperm, how many need
to have an "ideal" shape to pass the WHO

79
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:38,530
bar? Fifty? Thirty?

80
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,440
Four. Four out of a hundred!

81
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:45,780
Imagine a party with a hundred guys
in a room: if just four of them look

82
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:51,200
presentable, the WHO says, "Spot on,
this party is completely within normal

83
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:54,790
limits!" (Keep in mind,
some labs use different scales:

84
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,120
always check the reference range
printed on your own sheet.)

85
00:04:58,160 --> 00:05:02,720
But the casting under that microscope
is harsher than Paris Fashion Week!

86
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,670
"Head one millimeter too round?

87
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:07,200
Eliminated. Tail slightly coiled?

88
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,450
Sorry, doesn't fit the brand aesthetic."

89
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:14,480
Come on, it's a microscopic cell—we're
not asking it to walk the runway for

90
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,770
Dior, we're asking it to swim!

91
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:22,040
Even among future dads, 96% of the
candidates get bounced at the door

92
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:23,070
by the bouncer!

93
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:28,620
In fact, a major US study showed that
the results of fertile and infertile men

94
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:32,880
overlap massively: some future
dads have rock-bottom numbers,

95
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:37,500
while some men in the infertile group
have lab reports worthy of being framed in

96
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:42,120
the Louvre! Same thing when only
morphology is low while count and motility

97
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:47,620
are normal: thousands of IVF and
ICSI cycles show no clear drop in

98
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:48,710
pregnancy chances.

99
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:51,620
A low number, on its own, is a question.

100
00:05:51,660 --> 00:05:52,740
Not an answer.

101
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:56,400
So why do we ask you to repeat
the test three months later?

102
00:05:56,440 --> 00:06:00,560
Because today's sperm snitches on
what you were doing three months ago!

103
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:02,660
That's the factory production time.

104
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,530
You drop off a sample in October?

105
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:07,480
The embryologist can't look
into the microscope and say:

106
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:10,840
"Aha, somebody caught a
nasty flu back in July!"

107
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,780
But that July flu can
show up in the numbers.

108
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:18,420
A Danish study tracked twenty-seven
young men every single month for over a

109
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:23,120
year—imagine the small talk at that
lab—and showed that a bad fever can make

110
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:27,730
concentration nosedive three months later,
and that drop can be temporary.

111
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:33,780
That's why the 2026 UK guidelines
are crystal clear: if the first test

112
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:37,030
is abnormal, we recheck
three months later.

113
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:42,020
The only exception: if there are
no sperm at all (or almost none),

114
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:45,940
we don't wait three months—we
repeat the test right away.

115
00:06:45,980 --> 00:06:50,860
For that second test, stick to the
abstinence window and mention any recent

116
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:55,080
fever. And if the first is
low but the second is normal,

117
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,590
which one do we believe?

118
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,460
Neither one on its own!

119
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:03,380
One is you with the flu in pajamas,
the other is you in your Sunday suit:

120
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:06,940
we need the average alongside
your medical history.

121
00:07:06,980 --> 00:07:11,780
While waiting for that second test,
please, do not listen to the "bench-press

122
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:15,930
endocrinologists" at the gym:
"Bro, just take some testosterone,

123
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,910
it'll put nitro in the tank!"

124
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:23,180
Listen closely: the WHO actually
tested injectable testosterone…

125
00:07:23,220 --> 00:07:25,870
as male birth control!

126
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:31,900
In their 1990 study, nearly six out
of ten men ended up with zero sperm.

127
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:36,940
That "nitro boost" from your gym coach
is actually the handbrake pulled all the

128
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:42,540
way up in reverse! The guidelines are
categorical: never use testosterone to

129
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:44,230
boost a semen analysis.

130
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:48,600
If you're taking it—even "just
for the pecs"—tell your doctor.

131
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:51,840
When should you see a
urologist or an andrologist?

132
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:56,220
Way too often, I see couples where she
has been going through blood draws and

133
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:58,200
ultrasounds for six months…

134
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:01,170
I turn to him: "And your semen analysis?"

135
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:05,740
"Yeah doctor, I'll go next month, I've
got a huge PowerPoint to finish at the

136
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:09,230
office…" You'd think we were
asking him to donate a kidney!

137
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:14,000
A male factor is present in one
out of two infertile couples:

138
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:18,200
the man's workup happens at the same
time, not when the Prime Minister's

139
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,320
schedule clears up!

140
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:23,370
The roadmap is simple (exact
thresholds are on screen):

141
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:29,120
1. After two abnormal semen analyses:
a physical exam of the testicles

142
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,880
and a hormone blood panel.

143
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:35,290
2. If concentration stays very low:
chromosome analysis.

144
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:41,770
3. If there are no (or almost no)
sperm: after quick confirmation,

145
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:45,870
we also look for a tiny
anomaly on the Y chromosome.

146
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:50,820
Whether it's a traffic jam on the
highway (a blockage) or a factory running

147
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:56,020
slow, solutions exist: repairing
the passage, hormone treatment,

148
00:08:56,060 --> 00:09:00,870
or surgically retrieving sperm from
the epididymis or the testicle itself.

149
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:05,640
Nobody can guarantee 100%
success upfront, but it is a

150
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,570
serious, viable path.

151
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:12,370
Jokes aside, one absolute rule
that never waits for a lab test:

152
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:16,010
A lump in the testicle:
see a doctor promptly.

153
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:20,000
Sudden, severe pain:
that is an absolute emergency.

154
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:23,460
Forget the lab,
head straight to the ER or call

155
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:26,700
911, 999, or 112.

156
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:31,880
My view as a physician is clear:
the semen analysis is a starting point,

157
00:09:31,920 --> 00:09:36,500
never absolute proof—neither to
condemn you too early if it's low,

158
00:09:36,540 --> 00:09:41,320
nor to guarantee everything is fine if
it's normal while pregnancy still isn't

159
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:46,560
happening. What matters is a confirmed
result, read together as a couple with a

160
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:48,350
doctor and a proper exam.

161
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:52,150
Not standing alone in front of the
fridge zooming in on your pixels!

162
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:57,360
Next time a lab report yells at you in
bold, ask yourself just one question:

163
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,950
was that the first test, or the second?

164
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:03,590
Three questions to bring to your
doctor (they're in the description):

165
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:07,450
1. Has the result been
confirmed by a second test?

166
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:11,490
2. Do we need a physical exam
and a hormone blood test?

167
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:15,440
3. Should we consult a
urologist or an andrologist?

168
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:20,340
This content is for informational purposes
and does not replace an individual

169
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:21,830
medical evaluation.

170
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:27,240
And if your second test stays a little
low: what everyday habits actually affect

171
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:30,840
sperm quality? That's the topic
of the video popping up on your

172
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,150
screen right now!
